WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.730
<b>Road Closed for Chiba Inter-High
Road Race Preliminaries</b>

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.860
<b>Inter-High Preliminaries  Chiba</b>

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.810
It's Sohoku High School. 
Sohoku High School's here.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.790
Last year's champs sure are intense.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:13.660
That guy's huge.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:14.570
It's Imaizumi.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.290
That red! It's Naruko.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.780
Their captain Teshima, Aoyagi, and...

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.910
Last year's general 
classification winner, Onoda.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.820
<i>Teshima, don't think you'll 
win so easily this year.</i>

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.590
<i>I, Yanagida, ace of Kashiwa Higashi High School, 
will be going to the Inter-High.</i>

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.680
Huh? Who's the last guy?

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.670
It's a first-year.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.760
Kaburagi Issa of Kanamegawa Middle School.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.940
Kaburagi? I've never heard of him.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.670
But if he's a regular as a first-year...

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.940
Then he must be pretty strong.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.110
<i>Crap. I'm nervous.</i>

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.410
Your habits are rubbing off on me, Danchiku.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.940
<i>Oh, right. Danchiku's not here.</i>

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.160
Crap. My stomach hurts...

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.440
<i>Is Issa okay?</i>

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.630
<i>Whenever he's nervous,
it affects his stomach first.</i>

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.360
Kabu's always thinking by himself.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.340
Maybe he doesn't understand that 
Sohoku High School fights as a team.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.350
Kaburagi, are you okay?

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.750
I'm great.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:32.570
I see.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.970
Before the race, I want to ask you something.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:40.830
Kaburagi, what do you ride for?

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.580
Isn't it obvious?

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.940
I ride...

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.080
...to win!

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.670
We endure long, grueling 
races because of that goal.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.210
Am I wrong?

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.300
Endure, huh?

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.840
You're not wrong. It's a good answer.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:03.640
Okay, we're finished warming up.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.780
Meet inside the bus. We'll start the meeting.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:07.430
Yes, sir!

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:12.980
It's the genius Kaburagi's debut race.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.420
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:46.780
<b>Inter-High Preliminaries  Chiba</b>

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:49.010
<i>RIDE.12  Trouble!</i>

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.870
What do you mean you're the ace, first-year?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.940
And why are you agreeing to this, perm head?

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:56.290
Why not? He wants to do it.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:59.480
I promise I'll win this race.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.240
Fine. Let's see you do it.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.550
We'll support you as best we can, too.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.190
No, I won't need your support.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.680
I'll ride solo ahead of 
the pack until the end.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:15.930
<i>The Inter-High Road Race Preliminaries 
Chiba Race is starting!</i>

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.670
<i>The race will consist of ten laps 
on the six-kilometer course set up</i>

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:23.120
<i>inside the Chiba Sports Center.</i>

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:28.700
<i>Which high school will win this 
race and advance to the Inter-High?</i>

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.230
<i>My stomach's fine now.</i>

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:34.290
<i>Once the race starts,
I'm good to go. I'll do it.</i>

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.000
<i>I'll win.</i>

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.380
One guy jumped ahead!

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.100
It's Sohoku!

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:41.800
Don't let him go!

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.260
<i>I'm feeling good. I can do it.</i>

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.150
<i>Are you watching, Danchiku?</i>

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.430
<i>This first victory is mine.</i>

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.520
What? A flat tire!

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.130
W-Wait!

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.220
<i>I'm so, so, so unlucky.</i>

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:07.200
<i>I got a flat on the first lap. Damn it.</i>

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:09.500
<i>Should I head back to HQ?</i>

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.880
<i>No, that would take too long.</i>

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:15.190
<i>A bike is stopped at the two-kilometer mark.</i>

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.770
<i>It's Sohoku High School #106, Kaburagi.</i>

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.210
<i>It looks like his rear tire is flat.</i>

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.300
<i>The manager should bring me a wheel now.</i>

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.040
<i>If she cuts across the field, 
it's about a kilometer.</i>

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.720
<i>If I can just wait until then...</i>

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:30.550
<i>Wait?</i>

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:34.230
<i>How long will that take? 
How far will the pack travel in that time?</i>

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:36.880
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:38.850
What?

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.940
Senpai...

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:46.760
Wh-Why? Why are you stopping?

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:48.450
You're in the middle of a race!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.530
You're our ace in this race.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:54.040
We're riding to support you.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.370
What?

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.500
You're the one who said 
he wanted to be the ace.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.750
Oh, uh... looks like you weren't so lucky.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.260
But you can't help it if you have a flat.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.090
Our seniors used to say luck 
was part of the race, too.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:11.430
<i>Are they crazy? Why are they 
smiling under these circumstances?</i>

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.390
<i>This is the preliminary race.</i>

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.900
Please go! Just keep going!

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.140
If we don't win today,
we can't go to the Inter-High!

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.600
Who cares about me?

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.660
Kaburagi...

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.190
Last year's captain, Kinjou-san, said

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:28.860
this jersey is complete 
when all six are together.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.370
It doesn't matter how many there are!

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.340
This is a lap race.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:36.830
If you fall behind,
you're forced to drop out!

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:40.330
<i>The leaders are entering the home stretch.</i>

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.170
<b>Inter-High Preliminaries  Chiba{A: added}</b>

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.170
<i>They'll be entering their second lap shortly.</i>

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.770
The pack is coming. Hurry!

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:49.300
During the second stage 
of last year's Inter-High,

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:53.010
Onoda stopped and waited for 
a senior named Tadokoro-san.

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:57.380
He pulled the sick Tadokoro-san to the

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:00.230
Team Sohoku jerseys that 
were so far ahead of them.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.020
All six were united.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:06.180
Some guys would probably say 
that didn't mean anything.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:10.000
But after that, Tadokoro-san pulled the team.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.440
We depended on each other and worked together.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:17.040
In the end, Onoda was entrusted with the team's 
hopes and took our jersey to the finish line.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.790
I believe in the power of six.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.380
Thanks for waiting.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.750
The manager's here.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.430
Hurry. The leaders are 
just around the corner.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:30.510
We know.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.970
They're here.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:35.890
It's done.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:39.890
This team always likes to cut it close.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.770
Don't say that, Naruko.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:45.310
We've got all six. Let's go.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.080
Sohoku High School's moving again.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.650
Pedal as hard as you can!

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.070
Yeah!

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:57.890
They got away.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.330
But they're still within range.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.670
<i>You made a mistake, Teshima.</i>

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:05.840
<i>The race may have just started, but it's 
impossible to make up this distance.</i>

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:09.640
I'll overtake you on the remaining 
nine laps and force you to drop out.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.220
The Inter-High will be attended...

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.050
By us!

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:16.650
The guys behind us are raring to go.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.640
What are we going to do, Teshima-san?

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:21.730
I guess we don't have a choice.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.560
We'd better do our best.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:27.480
We need to catch up first 
to the group behind us.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:32.320
<i>Catch up? Are they serious?</i>

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:37.000
What?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.700
Sorry, Yanagida.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.120
Could you hold onto that for a while?

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:42.580
What?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.080
I'll come back for it later.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:48.380
Yeah, around the ninth lap.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:49.960
What?

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:53.350
Oh, right. You can drink it.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:54.800
It's probably heavy.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.100
Enjoy your tea time.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.560
T-Teshima!

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:05.390
<i>Has Teshima-senpai always been the kind 
of person who provokes people like that?</i>

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:07.870
Let's start catching up, Aoyagi.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:10.940
We'll ride at 80% to pull ahead.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:11.650
Got it.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:14.110
Let's start this game of tag.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:15.490
Yeah!

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.770
<i>We pulled ahead in a second.</i>

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.500
<i>Aoyagi-senpai's pulling is amazing.</i>

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.580
I haven't seen the evil 
Teshima-san in a while.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.210
What?

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:32.090
The ingenious strategies that once 
tortured us are going strong.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.020
Is that a compliment?

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.140
The group is scary because it's a group.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:41.050
But if you break them apart, it's not.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:44.470
Damn it! We'll catch up 
no matter what, Teshima!

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:46.330
Don't underestimate us, Sohoku High School!

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:51.060
My declaration that we'll catch up
 will break the group apart.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.990
With fewer riders, the pack will slow down.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.450
They're wasting their chance to pass us.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:01.390
<i>All that thought was behind 
that performance of his?</i>

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:02.620
Besides...

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:05.730
We have all six of our members.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:06.830
<i>Six.</i>

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.960
Yanagida, we're overpacing ourselves.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.300
At this pace, we won't even
finish the race, let alone win.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.420
Shut up. We just have to catch 
up to Sohoku High School.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.390
I'll pull them out of the race!

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:25.050
It's a little early, but let's do it, Aoyagi.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.850
Got it. We'll go at 100%.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.570
Ultimate technique...

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:39.360
The improved version of Tadokoro-san's 
Sohoku High School Human Bullet Train.

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:50.580
The Supersonic Oxygen 
Human Bullet Aoyagi Train!

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.950
<i>He's fast. I can't believe how fast he is.</i>

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:58.420
<i>I can barely keep up.</i>

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:00.900
<i>Tadokoro-san, are you watching?</i>

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.330
<i>I'm finally going to the Inter-High.</i>

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:04.300
<i>And...</i>

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.480
<i>I'll win.</i>

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.110
Th-They're fast.

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:13.490
I can't catch up.

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:15.020
Sohoku High School's too strong.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.550
<i>As we enter the ninth lap 
of this ten-lap race,</i>

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:31.670
<b>Inter-High Preliminaries  Chiba</b>

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:31.670
<i>Sohoku High School has finally 
caught up to the leaders.</i>

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.950
<i>Amazing. We really did catch up.</i>

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:37.250
<i>And on the ninth lap, just like he said.</i>

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.510
<i>The fans are intoxicated by 
this dramatic turn of events.</i>

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:44.010
<i>The pack is completely 
overwhelmed by this atmosphere.</i>

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:48.030
Teshima-san, did you predict this, too?

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:52.070
Sorry, Yanagida. I'm back 
for my water bottle.

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:54.100
Take it.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:56.310
Don't make too much of it.

00:11:57.530 --> 00:12:01.570
There's one lap left. You're up now.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.160
Me?

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:05.820
We'll take you to the finish line.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.460
Ride like your life depends on it.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:08.910
I-Imaizumi-san?

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.490
I told you, you're the ace today.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.120
Your job is to take the finish line.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.620
Whatever you do, don't fall behind.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:21.510
Yes, sir.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:24.250
<i>He's fast. He's perfectly efficient.</i>

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:26.500
<i>He accelerates so beautifully.</i>

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:30.030
A-Are you okay?

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.200
He told you not to fall behind.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:35.270
Since you're the ace,
pedal until your nose bleeds.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.520
Yes, sir!

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:43.240
<i>Incredible. Naruko-san's 
accelerating as he pushes me.</i>

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:44.890
You can do it.

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:45.820
<i>Onoda-san!</i>

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.310
That's it. Pedal hard, Kabu.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:53.580
Just so you know, the Inter-High's 
a hundred times harder than this!

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:00.530
Let's go!

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:01.460
Yes, sir!

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:18.980
<b>Inter-High Preliminaries  Chiba</b>

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:15.120
<i>Goal! Sohoku High School wins 
the Chiba preliminaries again.</i>

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:18.980
<i>Taking first through sixth place, 
they've achieved a perfect victory.</i>

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:26.060
<i>Amazing. I got a flat and fell behind,
but I actually took first.</i>

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:29.430
<i>Team Sohoku is amazing.</i>

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:35.360
Naruko-san, Imaizumi-san, thank you.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.890
Don't forget to thank 
Teshima-san and Aoyagi-san.

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:42.400
Get up there and show the fans your jersey.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.760
The man who receives the most 
praise in a road race...

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:48.470
...is the one who crosses the finish line first.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:55.140
<i>I... I joined the greatest team.</i>

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:58.990
<i>I feel like our form is great now.</i>

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:02.260
<i>I feel like we're really unified.</i>

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:04.070
Hey, Naruko-kun.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:08.260
I actually wanted to take first, though.

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:08.870
What?

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.730
The finish line was right 
in front of me. Darn it...

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:12.580
What?

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:15.160
Ace, my butt. Who does he think he is?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.330
Why did we have to let 
him take the finish line?

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.870
Hey, hotshot. We agree for once.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:23.750
Starting today, his nickname is "showoff."{A: orig "hothead," making change per TL's suggestion. I think the lines just make more sense if you do the nickname this way.}

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:24.340
<i>What?</i>

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:28.610
What? But I was just thinking 
the team's in great form.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:29.970
This is fine.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:30.620
What?

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:33.460
First place is special.

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:35.400
No one wants to give it up.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.080
Not even to a teammate or a junior.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:39.630
But...

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.840
It's okay if they don't get along.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:42.480
What?

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:45.860
The determination to not
lose holds them together.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:51.440
Even if they bicker normally,
when things get tough and they can't ride,

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:53.240
<b>Certain</b>

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.240
they'll turn it around in a second.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:57.850
Riders determined not to lose 
give the team strength.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:00.940
"Don't follow me," becomes, "Keep up."

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:04.000
And that connection causes miracles.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:06.840
That's what I believe.

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:08.920
<i>I see.</i>

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:13.150
<i>That's this year's Sohoku High School.</i>

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:18.930
Listen up. Starting today, you're "showoff."

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:23.130
If you've got anything to say, you can 
say it once you can keep up with us.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:26.900
Understood! I accept!

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:30.610
I'll practice super hard 
and surpass you someday!

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:34.280
Imaizumi Shunsuke,
I promise I'll surpass you!

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:37.690
Are you going to say that to everyone?

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:39.960
Naruko Shoukichi, I'll surpass you, too!

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.340
I'll be waiting.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:46.460
He said the same thing to you, didn't he?

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:52.210
Finally, why do you race?

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:55.560
Today, when I crossed the 
finish line, I had a thought.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.880
That I'm riding for my team.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:03.060
But I was wrong!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.200
It's to win! That's all!

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:06.830
That's my only motivation!

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.450
He's really glaring at us.

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:13.250
But he's finally showing 
his true colors, I guess.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.610
Yeah.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.160
The champions, Sohoku High School...

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.960
They certainly are strong.

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:21.910
It's going to be another 
hot summer this year.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.420
This is seriously bad.

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:27.270
Sohoku High School had a perfect finish.

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:29.460
They're going to be strong, Midousuji-kun.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.760
The vermin champions, huh?

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:36.870
Good.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:37.680
What?

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.670
The more perfect they are,
the weaker they are.

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:45.080
The riper the fruit, the sooner it falls.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.150
But it's okay. I found a weakness.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:54.380
I, Mizuta Nobuyuki, as the new captain of 
Kyoto Fushimi High School, will... huh?

00:16:58.570 --> 00:17:05.120
Don't worry, zaku. I've gotten 
stronger this year, too.

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:09.680
And I have you.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:16.970
Midousuji-san, your muscles are looking 
great today. They're excellent.

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:19.560
I'm exhausted.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.800
Hey, Komari. Massage me again today.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:23.850
Yes, sir.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.900
It really works.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.970
<i>These muscles are the worst.</i>

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:37.280
<i>They think he's a simple masseuse.</i>

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.850
<i>But let the small fry think that.</i>

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.710
It's finally time for practice.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.000
I always wash my hands...

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:54.130
Before I ride you.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.210
Okay, perfect.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:10.020
I feel great when my bike's sparkling clean.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.900
It's so hot. Summer's coming soon.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:18.780
And with it, the Inter-High.

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:26.660
We'll get to ride together again, Manami-kun.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:30.970
Huh? The call light is on.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.670
<b>One Missed Call
Manami Sangaku-kun</b>

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:33.670
Manami-kun?

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:37.130
Why? He never calls me.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:44.110
S-Sorry, Manami-kun. I didn't 
notice my phone was ringing.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:44.110
<i>This number could not be 
answered at this time.</i>

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:48.900
<i>At the tone, please leave 
your name and message.</i>

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:48.430
It's his answering machine...

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:52.800
Uh, this is Onoda. Thanks for calling.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:54.610
We're going to the race.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:57.480
I hope we get to ride together again.

00:18:58.420 --> 00:18:59.740
I'm looking forward to it.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:03.030
Yeah, so am I.

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:06.690
Manami-kun? H-How?

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:09.220
<i>I answered because you called.</i>

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:11.430
<i>It took me a while, though.</i>

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:13.790
Oh, right.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:17.730
We won our prefecture's preliminary, too.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:25.430
Touched by an Angel

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:20.420
Izumida-san was really into it.

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:22.670
We finished ten minutes ahead 
of the second place team.

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:24.450
They say it's a new race record.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:25.430
<i>That's amazing.</i>

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:29.320
<i>Oh, no, no. That's not why I called.</i>

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:31.120
<i>Where do you think I am right now?</i>

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:32.020
What?

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:36.020
It's a place you told me you like.

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:37.190
Could it be?

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:38.230
Yeah.

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.570
I'm in Akihabara.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.070
<i>Akiba...</i>

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:45.790
We're on our way to check 
out the Inter-High course,

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:50.790
but we stopped by because a senior named 
Ashikiba-san forgot his phone charger.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:54.750
<i>Manami-kun's in Akiba... 
Manami-kun's in Akiba...</i>

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:56.790
<i>Anyway, this place is crowded. 
It's like a festival.</i>

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:58.170
I'll be right there.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:00.610
<i>What? Sorry, but we won't be 
here longer than ten minutes.</i>

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:02.300
I'll still go.

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:22.550
I'm an idiot.

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:31.370
<b>Hakone
Academy
High
School</b>

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:33.780
Manami-kun...

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:38.740
<i>Deliver my bottle to me again, Sakamichi-kun.</i>

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.560
<i>This time, I'll accept it with a smile.</i>

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:47.180
Thanks for letting me come along with you.

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:52.020
It's fine. Since it'll save time,
it helps us, too.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.230
I appreciate you saying that.

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:57.980
So, do you think you can beat 
Sohoku High School this year?

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:02.810
The question isn't whether or 
not we can beat them. It's—

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:06.410
That's right. It's whether or 
not they can keep up with us.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:10.380
We're Hakone Academy High School.

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:12.950
It won't take me a second to crush them.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:15.140
That's enough, Doubashi.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:17.760
I know I've said this before,

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:21.050
but all six members of Sohoku 
Academy High School are aces.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.430
Let me be clear.

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:29.760
Last year they took the title of champions 
from us, but we haven't lost our pride.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:33.180
We're strong. And...

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:37.260
I am strong.

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:14.740
Onoda-san, let me hold your basket.

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:17.080
These gummies are really good.

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:19.740
Onoda-san, let's get some 
ice cream. It's hot out.

00:23:19.740 --> 00:23:21.830
Yeah, okay. They look good.

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:22.540
What should we get?

00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:26.120
It's gotta be Papeko. We can split one.

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:28.380
You look like you're having fun, showoff.

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:30.130
We're getting Papeko, too.

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:33.890
Let's get donuts instead, Onoda-san.

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:35.680
Do you really hate us that much?

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.890
<i>NEXT RIDE  1000km Again</i>

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:44.900
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
